A||||16||loafer87gt||Grumpy old men||||1||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||12-17-2000||09:47 PM||||I had to go to the pet store yesterday to get my cat some fud, and while I was throwing the 10KG bag in the cab of my truck, I brushed my horn in the truck. An old guy was getting out of his car besides me, and the horn scared him causing him to slip on the ice. I kinda gave him a sheapish look, as it was just an accident, but he totally freaked out on me. Next thing I know, I have a 70+ year old guy pounding on my passenger window calling me a F'in young punk with no respect amongst several other unpleasant names. He ranted on for quite sometime before I got worried he was gonna kick in the side of my truck or break my window, so I just threw my truck in drive and left the grumpy old fart standing there. Man, I know I have some days when I'm in a bad mood, but this is ridiculous!  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||2xsess||12-17-2000||10:14 PM||||Grumpy Old people suck. I dealt with a bunch of them in South FL.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||13
Z||000002||fiero56||12-18-2000||12:10 AM||||I speak this for most all old people. They always think everyone is out to get them, isn't that a skitzoid?? People are out to harm them, take their money, waste their time waiting in lines, rip them off, etc, etc, etc...<BR>Yesterday while in a parking lot, one old man didn't see a stop sign and ran through it, another old man almost t-boned him. They finally ended up giving each other the finger, repeatedly, shouting obsenities at each other, etc. I was returning a cable convertor the other day, and the old guy in front of me complained of having to wait in line 10 minutes, and wouldn't shut up. He mentioned the place was out to waste the time of senior citezins on purpose and other such non-sense. <BR>---------<BR>Stay home!<BR>Sit down!<BR>Shut up!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||RaeQwan||12-18-2000||05:02 AM||||but they arn't out to waste us young pppls time are they? hehe<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/raeqwanegg.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||hugh||12-18-2000||07:36 AM||||56,What do you consider old?I'm almost 61,and you sure as hell don't speak for me.Maybe it's because I own a Fiero and my state of mind is such that I am happy with my place in this world.It annoys me when someone makes blanket statements about a segment of the population,or a specific group without the experience that comes with being a part of that group.I know that you are speaking from your experiences,but do you really believe that? ||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||12-18-2000||08:44 AM||||I know and have met some pretty cool "older people", but there are so many of them that are always grumpy or waiting to attack you for the smallest infraction. It's like they are just waiting for you to give them a reason to go off the deep end. If I am approaching a stop-sign, and almost at a dead stop(an inch an hour), if you're not looking at that old person approaching from the right or left with the right-of-way, they lay it on that horn, give the finger, etc... Happens almost every day here.<P>Hugh, 61 is much younger than I am speaking of. Maybe I should use a different term(anybody remember the original term for "little people" until it wasn't politically correct?). Senior citezin starts at 55(I think) and that is younger than those to which I was referring. I'll have to think up a politically appealing term.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Wolfhound||12-18-2000||08:55 AM||||Guy,s here is a site about grumpy old men you will really enjoy.<P>Twenty six WWII Veterans are sailing a WWII LST (Landing Ship Tank) across the Atlantic. Average age over 70.<P>The site is a day by day log of their voyage. they have Departed Gibralta and will have several stops along the east coast as they travel south to to the keys and into the Gulf of Mexico. <P>You can read their daily report and track their progress if you like.<P>Their final destination is Mobile Bay where the LST will become a floating museum along side the Battle Ship Alabama at Battle Ship Park.<P>Several of us are planning on going down and escourting them into mobile Bay as the 55 year old ship arrives.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.palosverdes.com/lst887/lst325.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.palosverdes.com/lst887/lst325.html</A> <P>Lets be a little more tolerant, OK!<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 12-18-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000007||Cooter||12-18-2000||09:11 AM||||This reminds me of a passage from my unpublished book, A hundred and one things my old grand daddy used to say:<BR>Stop laughing at my legs boy! When you get to be my age, you might need suspenders to hold your socks up too.<P>I don't know why I could never get that book published.||||reg||1
Z||000008||stimpy||12-18-2000||09:19 AM||||Will they have the left blinker on the whole way?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Really, this stereotype about geriatrics being impatient and prne to complain can be applied to just about any segment of society. I cannot get into a line of any duration without someone getting pissy for waiting. Perhaps older people just don't give a **** avout what people think, so they are more likely to get vocal if they think it will do something.  But I have heard the same laments come from people of all ages and socio-economic standing.  And it never fails to bug the crap out of me...||||reg||1
Z||000009||Tigger||12-18-2000||10:01 AM||||Maybe that's the reason why the Eskimo's use to send their elders off on ice floats? j/k<P>I hate to see stereotypes put on our elder generation too.  Makes you wonder if people realize that if they live long enough they will be old too?<P>Don't take it personal, he must have thought you were just another one of those little whipper snappers.  Doesn't take much to "set someone off" at any age these days.||||reg||1
Z||000010||ChadMan||12-18-2000||11:20 AM||||I have a theory about this topic...stupid and bitchy old people didn't become stupid and bitchy simply because they got old.  Chances are they were always stupid and bitchy and it's just more pronounced now that they're old!<P>There are plenty of bright old folks who fit just fine into modern society.  You just don't notice them as much because they're not a pain in your a$$!  You don't notice the old guy driving the speed limit in the right lane - just the one driving 10 below in the passing lane, keeping you from reaching your destination.<P>Look at the Florida election.  I'd have to guess the overwhelming majority of old folks down there had no problem whatsoever voting for their chosen candidate.  But smart old people aren't newsworthy - just the idiots.||||reg||1
Z||000011||hugh||12-18-2000||12:44 PM||||Chadman,You hit the nail on the head.Some people are just miserable from the word go,and some people feel that when they get to a certain age that the world owes them something.||||reg||1
Z||000012||2xsess||12-18-2000||01:29 PM||||I didn't mean to offend anyone.<P>That was why I stated "<B>Grumpy</B> Old people suck"<P>I used to have a 71 year old formaer Marine working for me when I was 18 and he and I'd sit around and BS for hours. There was also a 75 year old guy that would help out sometimes too and he was a mason who had lots of stories to tell.<BR>So I'm not making a blanket statment. I just wanted to clear that up. I realized it after I posted and it's been bugging me.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||batboy||12-18-2000||05:02 PM||||I can be a grumpy old man at times too. You get tired of the crap that goes on and get to the point where you ain't going to take anymore crap from people without dishing out some crap of your own. Of course, many people go way too far.<P>Just be glad that was a grumpy old man that got mad at you. If it had been one of those young hot-headed crack smoking gang members, he might of pulled out an Uzi and popped off a clip at you.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Raydar||12-18-2000||05:09 PM||||This isn't meant as a support OR rebuttal to anything that was posted previously. Merely an observation.<P>I have found that the older I get (43 now), the lower my "bu11sh!t" tolerance is. Not willing to let stuff slide, like I used to. <BR>On the other hand, I'm not nearly as outspoken about stuff that doesn't affect me, directly. <BR>Anybody else noticed this about themself?<P>Raydar||||reg||1
